Situation:
Regional depots are holding limited stocks for near-term distribution to dispersed maneuver and support units operating from forward locations. Lines of communication include primary and secondary main supply routes, a valley corridor exposed to ambush, and a contested river crossing that requires engineer support when used. Security conditions, distance, and terrain drive route-by-route transport costs and movement windows across the planning horizon. Depot throughput is constrained; forward units have time-phased demands that must be met to sustain current operations. Fleet availability and per-vehicle carrying capacity are limiting factors. If demand cannot be fully met on a given day, controlled shortfalls are allowed but carry readiness penalties. Activating any depot-to-unit route on a given day (sending any vehicles) incurs a fixed Risk Cost to cover escorts, route clearance, and quick-reaction force posture, regardless of the number of vehicles subsequently dispatched on that route.

Mission:
Deliver required supplies from regional depots to all designated forward units over the planning horizon while minimizing total operational cost, defined as the sum of route transport costs, shortage penalties for unmet demand, vehicle deployment costs, and fixed route security Risk Costs. Maintain convoy security, preserve fleet readiness, and remain within depot release limits and fleet capacity constraints.

Execution/Concept:
- Depot constraints: Daily shipments from each depot will not exceed available stock and throughput. Allocation will be synchronized with anticipated route availability and security posture.
- Demand fulfillment: Each unit’s day-specific requirement will be met from any combination of depots; controlled shortfalls are permitted only when required by risk, capacity, or stock constraints and accrue penalty costs.
- Vehicle employment: Total vehicles available per day are limited. Each convoy’s lifted load is bounded by per-vehicle capacity and the volumetric factor of the supply being moved. Vehicle deployment incurs a per-vehicle operating cost.
- Route activation and risk: Vehicles may only move on routes activated for that day. Activating a route incurs a fixed Risk Cost (escorts, route clearance, overwatch) independent of convoy size; additional vehicles on an already activated route do not increase this fixed component. The plan will concentrate movements on a minimal set of safe, efficient routes where tactically acceptable to limit fixed risk overhead while preserving redundancy for critical units.
- Transport costs: Route-specific movement costs vary by depot-to-unit pairing and by day. The distribution plan will favor lower-cost corridors unless risk, timing, or capacity dictates alternatives.
- Priorities and controls: Priority of support will be given to mission-critical units and time-sensitive requirements. Movement Control will track vehicle assignments per route and day, ensuring the total employed fleet remains within limits. Dynamic retasking is authorized if routes close or threats escalate.

